Hey, I'll try to be very brief:

1.)

You're mixing the imperial and the metric system, which is very hard to read.

Stick to the metric system for the foundation's sake. You can always write foot in brackets.

2.)



It shows very little muscle mass, arms are out of proportion with the rest of the body, the subject has shown to have no signs of hair, eyes, nose, its mouth can open up to two (2) times the norm of a normal human
附加记录：    

Sounds like SCP-096 to me! Unfortunately this concept is pretty overused, although I like the idea of no eyes, hair, nose, etc

3.)



Attempting to kill SCP-5913 []
附加记录：    

Wow, that escalated quickly!

4.)

Do the 87km/h in 3087km/h and the 176km/h in 6176km/h really matter?

Lots of people ruin their stories by being overly specific - and if your SCP can break the sound barrier 5 times, you don't need to be specific! You can just write Mach-5 for example.

5.)



[] the subject prefers to teleport rather than running because of exhausted
附加记录：    

First - because of exhaustion

Second - So why running, when it can teleport? And if it is just that fast, then you would have an ear-deafening sound every time it moves because of physics.

6.)



The subject is not invulnerable it can still injured
附加记录：    

The subject is not invulnerable and can still be injured.

You should always proof read. There are a lot of spelling errors in your text in general.

7.)



Its presence causes several negative effects on the minds of its targets including inhibiting memory loss while also adding memory, altering sense and perception of a person’s environment, influencing a person’s personality very negatively such as causing a great deal of paranoia, nightmares, and hallucinations, etc.
附加记录：    

I won't go any further than that, since I get the feeling that you also don't know where this is going. So you have a teleporting (sometimes running), mind affecting SCP-096 with tendrils. What?

I hope I wasn't too harsh with the critisism here, but if I was in your shoes, I'd just leave it and invent a new story. ;)







